0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                             ;  B8Script interpreter for the Z80
0000                             ;  Spec: docs/b8script.md (2026-11-21).
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Three switches, set in the EQU lines below:
0000                             ;    CPM      0 = generic ROM build (KEY/CONOUT at fixed addresses)
0000                             ;             1 = CP/M 2.2 .COM file: loads the file named on the command line
0000                             ;    EDITOR   1 = with the line editor built in (see the end of this file):
0000                             ;                 the spec's suggested standard. It goes with either setting
0000                             ;                 of the other two.
0000                             ;    CHECKED  0 = no checks (spec: the programmer is responsible)
0000                             ;             1 = starts with every variable at 0 and every word undefined,
0000                             ;                 and stops on every error in the spec's table (and Ctrl-C)
0000                             ;                 with a four-line report: the letter and the place as line
0000                             ;                 and column, the text there, and both stacks. See `error`.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  In every build Ctrl-C stops a running program (an unchecked build stops
0000                             ;  without a word): see the console layer for the rules, the held key and
0000                             ;  the break-off cell.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Assembler: asm80 (https://maly.github.io/asm80-node/), Z80 mode.
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                CPM:      EQU   1   ; 1 = CP/M .COM build
0000                CHECKED:   EQU   0   ; 1 = checked build
0000                EDITOR:   EQU   0   ; 1 = with the line editor
0000                EDGEN:    EQU   EDITOR*(1-CPM)   ; (the generic build with the editor)
0000                             ; (IF takes any value but 0 as true, so
0000                             ;  IF CHECKED+EDITOR means "either")
0000                TABP0:    EQU   EDGEN*(1-CHECKED)   ; (the build with its table in page zero)
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ;  Register use, everywhere in the interpreter
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    BC   IP: the address of the next program character to read
0000                             ;    HL   TOS: the top data-stack cell is kept here, not in memory
0000                             ;    SP   the data stack: (SP) is NOS, the cell under TOS. The data stack is
0000                             ;         the Z80"s own stack, which is what the spec"s machine-code contract
0000                             ;         needs ("the data cells above the return address").
0000                             ;    HL'  return-stack pointer (the alternate HL). Entries are 2 bytes; the
0000                             ;         stack grows down. Only rpop and rpushn (and the checks) touch it.
0000                             ;    A DE scratch. Every handler is entered with HL = TOS and may use A, DE.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  One-byte calls. The routines used most are reached with RST, one byte
0000                             ;  instead of three:
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    RST 08h  rpop    pop the return stack into DE
0000                             ;    RST 18h  drop    drop TOS, then next character     (ends a handler)
0000                             ;    RST 20h  neg16   HL = -HL
0000                             ;    RST 28h  putc    print A
0000                             ;    RST 30h  next    next character                    (ends a handler)
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  RST 18h and RST 30h never return: an RST is a CALL, so the first thing
0000                             ;  each of them does is POP DE to throw the return address away.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  The CP/M build can't own page zero, so the block from `vecs` to `vecend`
0000                             ;  (image addresses 0108h-0133h) is copied to 0008h-0033h when it starts. The
0000                             ;  code in that block is written to work at either place.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Dispatch. PTAB holds one byte per punctuation character: the low byte of
0000                             ;  its handler's address. The high byte is worked out from the character:
0000                             ;  the handlers of the first NPG1 characters (in code order) start in the
0000                             ;  image's second page, the rest in its first. The layout below keeps to
0000                             ;  that, and testing/chktab.py checks it in every build.
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ;  Memory map. Everything the interpreter writes is in four RAM pages:
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    RSPAGE   return stack, 112 entries (the pointer stays inside this page)
0000                             ;    DSPAGE   data stack, 127 cells (the top four bytes of the page are spare,
0000                             ;             so a full stack runs two bytes into the page below)
0000                             ;    LETPAGE  letter cells: A..Z at +00h..+33h, a..z at +40h..+73h (so a word
0000                             ;             cell is always 64 bytes below its variable), the heap pointer at
0000                             ;             +7Ch, interpreter variables in the gaps, and the -n? line buffer
0000                             ;             at +80h..+FFh
0000                             ;    PROG     the program text, NUL-terminated; the heap starts after the NUL
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  The stacks sit below the letter page, so "the program's own space" (what
0000                             ;  the checked build lets ! and . write) is the single range from the letter
0000                             ;  page up to the heap limit. Each stack has a guard band: the data stack can
0000                             ;  overrun by a cell or two (and the calls made while it is full, the error
0000                             ;  report's included) into the top 32 bytes of the return-stack page, which
0000                             ;  are never used, and the return stack by one entry into the page below it.
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                          IF   CPM   
0000                BDOS:     EQU   0005h   
0000                BASE:     EQU   0100h   ; where the image starts
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   CPM*(1-EDITOR)   
0000                EXIT:     EQU   0000h   ; warm boot
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IFN   CPM   
                                 ; ---- generic machine: edit these to suit -----------------------------------
                    KEY:      EQU   0FF06h   ; a waiting key in A, or A = 0 if none is
                                 ;   waiting. The zero flag must match A
                                 ;   (end the routine with OR A / RET).
                    CONOUT:   EQU   0FF03h   ; print the character in A
                                 ;   KEY and CONOUT must preserve BC, DE, HL and HL'.
                    RSPAGE:   EQU   80h   ; 8000h return stack
                    DSPAGE:   EQU   81h   ; 8100h data stack
                    LETPAGE:   EQU   82h   ; 8200h letter cells and line buffer
                    PROG:     EQU   8300h   ; where the loader puts the program text
                    HEAPLIM:   EQU   0F0h   ; the heap must stay below F000h (a page)
                    BASE:     EQU   0000h   ; where the image starts
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)   
                    EXIT:     EQU   0FF09h   ; where to go when the program ends
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   EDGEN   
                    LEAVE:    EQU   0FF09h   ; where the editor's ^X goes
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   EDITOR*CPM   
                    LEAVE:    EQU   0000h   ; the editor's ^X: warm boot
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   EDITOR   
                    EXIT:     EQU   edend   ; a program that ends goes back to the editor,
                    SKEND:    EQU   skend   ;   also when it ends inside skip
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   1-EDITOR   
0000                SKEND:    EQU   EXIT   
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                MSLOOP:   EQU   40   ; n? inner loop count for about 1 ms (1-255):
0000                             ; each pass calls getk once, so tune it for
0000                             ; your clock and your KEY routine. (The wait
0000                             ; for a second Ctrl-C uses it too: 250 ms.)
0000                             ; letter-page layout (offsets inside LETPAGE)
0000                LET:      EQU   LETPAGE*256   
0000                HEAP:     EQU   LET+7Ch   ; the heap pointer
0000                RSAVE:    EQU   LET+34h   ; gap after Z: return stack pointer, saved
0000                             ;   around machine code;
0000                NPEND:    EQU   LET+38h   ;   minus the address of the program's end
0000                             ;   (the heap"s first byte), for the checked "_';
0000                EDLN:     EQU   LET+3Ah   ;   the editor: the number of the line that ^E
0000                             ;   put in the input line (0: none)
0000                KEYBUF:   EQU   LET+7Ah   ; gap after z: a key read by the break check and
0000                             ;   held for the next "?" (0: none);
0000                BRKOFF:   EQU   LET+7Bh   ;   the break-off cell: a program that stores a
0000                             ;   non-zero byte here gets Ctrl-C as a key
0000                LBHDR:    EQU   LET+7Eh   ; CP/M BDOS 10 header: max, count
0000                LINEBUF:   EQU   LET+80h   ; -n? text, ending in CR
0000                RSTOP:    EQU   RSPAGE*256+0E0h   ; empty return stack: the 32 bytes above it
0000                             ; take calls made while the data stack is full
0000                DSTOP:    EQU   DSPAGE*256+0FCh   ; empty data stack. The four bytes above it
0000                             ; are spare: a character can pop two cells
0000                             ; too many before the checked build sees it,
0000                             ; and the next call must not land on the
0000                             ; letter cells.
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                             ;  The first 49 bytes: the entry, then the RST routines, with small handlers
0000                             ;  and routines filling the gaps between them. Generic: this IS page zero.
0000                             ;  CP/M: it is the start of the .COM file, and 0108h-0133h is also copied to
0000                             ;  page zero (see the header).
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0100                          .ORG   BASE   
0100                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)*CHECKED   
                              XOR   A   ; 00  reset. (This byte, AFh, is also what an
0100                          ENDIF      ;     undefined word runs into: see e_hi.)
0100                          IF   1-EDGEN   
0100   31 FC 06               LD   SP,DSTOP   ; 00  reset, or the start of the .COM file
0103                          ENDIF      
0103                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)*(1-CHECKED)   
                              LD   BC,PROG   ; 03  the IP
                              JR   st0   ; 06  (the rest of the startup is close by)
0103                          ENDIF      
0103                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)*CHECKED   
                              JR   init   ; 04  (the rest of the startup is close by)
                              DW   0   ; 06  spare
0103                          ENDIF      
0103                          IF   EDGEN   
                              XOR   A   ; 00  reset: no program yet. (This byte, AFh,
                              LD   (PROG),A   ;     is also what an undefined word runs
                              JP   init   ; 04  into in the checked build: see e_hi.)
                              NOP      ; 07  spare
0103                          ENDIF      
0103                          IF   CPM   
0103   C3 07 04               JP   start   ; 03
0106   00 00                  DW   0   ; 06  spare
0108                          ENDIF      
0108                VECS:        
0108                             ; ---- RST 08h: rpop: pop the return stack into DE ---------------------------
0108   D9           RPOP:     EXX      ; 08
0109   5E                     LD   E,(HL)   
010A   23                     INC   HL   
010B   56                     LD   D,(HL)   
010C   23                     INC   HL   
010D   D5                     PUSH   DE   ; across to the main registers
010E   D9                     EXX      
010F   D1                     POP   DE   
0110   C9                     RET      ; 10  (so RST 10h is not used)
0111                             ; ctl: the inner loop comes here for characters below 21h. A = c - 21h.
0111   C6 21        CTL:      ADD   A,21h   ; 11  back to c; zero only for NUL
0113   20 1F                  JR   NZ,next0   ;     the rest are ignored
0115   C3 00 00     ENDPROG:   JP   EXIT   ;     the program has ended
0118                             ; ---- RST 18h: drop TOS, then next ------------------------------------------
0118   D1           RST18:    POP   DE   ; 18  discard the RST's return address
0119   E1                     POP   HL   ;     new TOS = NOS
011A   18 15                  JR   nx   
011C   E5           H_FROMR:   PUSH   HL   ; 1C  "}" return stack to TOS
011D   CF                     RST   08h   
011E   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
011F   F7                     RST   30h   
0120                             ; ---- RST 20h: neg16: HL = -HL (keeps BC, DE) -------------------------------
0120   AF           NEG16:    XOR   A   ; 20
0121   95                     SUB   L   
0122   6F                     LD   L,A   
0123   9F                     SBC   A,A   
0124   94                     SUB   H   
0125   67                     LD   H,A   
0126   C9                     RET      
0127   00                     NOP      ; 27  spare
0128                             ; ---- RST 28h: putc: print A (keeps BC, DE, HL, HL') ------------------------
0128                RST28:       
0128                          IFN   CPM   
                    PUTC:     JP   CONOUT   ; 28
0128                          ENDIF      
0128                          IF   CPM   
0128   C3 EE 03               JP   putc   ; 28
012B                          ENDIF      
012B   E9           JPHL:     JP   (HL)   ; 2B  (for the machine-code call)
012C   E3           H_TOR:    EX   (SP),HL   ; 2C  "{" TOS to the return stack: the new TOS
012D   C3 C1 01               JP   rpushn   ;     comes up, the old one goes across
0130                             ; ---- RST 30h: next character -----------------------------------------------
0130   D1           RST30:    POP   DE   ; 30  discard the RST's return address
0131                NX:          
0131                          IF   CPM   
0131   C3 34 01               JP   next0   ; (this copy runs in page zero)
0134                          ENDIF      
0134                VECEND:      
0134                             ; =============================================================================
0134                             ;  The inner loop: read one character and sort it by range.
0134                             ; 
0134                             ;    00h          end of program
0134                             ;    01h-20h, 7Fh-FFh   ignored (control, space, DEL, high bytes)
0134                             ;    30h-39h      digit: read a whole number
0134                             ;    41h-5Ah      A-Z: call the word in that letter's cell
0134                             ;    61h-7Ah      a-z: push the address of that letter's cell
0134                             ;    the rest     punctuation: jump through PTAB, 32 entries, in code order
0134                             ; =============================================================================
0134                NEXT0:       
0134                          IF   CHECKED   
                              CALL   chkstk   ; both stacks are checked once per character
0134                          ENDIF      
0134   0A                     LD   A,(BC)   
0135   03                     INC   BC   
0136   D6 21                  SUB   21h   ; A = c - 21h
0138   38 D7                  JR   C,ctl   ; c < 21h: NUL ends, the rest are ignored
013A   FE 0F                  CP   0Fh   
013C   38 22                  JR   C,punct   ; 21h-2Fh: PTAB index 0-14
013E   D6 0F                  SUB   0Fh   ; A = c - 30h
0140   FE 0A                  CP   0Ah   
0142   38 67                  JR   C,digit   ; 30h-39h
0144   FE 11                  CP   11h   
0146   38 16                  JR   C,p3a   ; 3Ah-40h
0148   D6 11                  SUB   11h   ; A = c - 41h
014A   FE 1A                  CP   1Ah   
014C   38 69                  JR   C,upper   ; 41h-5Ah: A = letter index 0-25
014E   FE 20                  CP   20h   
0150   38 0A                  JR   C,p5b   ; 5Bh-60h
0152   FE 3A                  CP   3Ah   
0154   38 5B                  JR   C,lower   ; 61h-7Ah: A = 20h-39h (cell +64 bytes)
0156   FE 3E                  CP   3Eh   
0158                          IF   1-CHECKED   
0158   30 DA                  JR   NC,next0   ; 7Fh-FFh: ignored
015A                          ENDIF      
015A                          IF   CHECKED   
                              JR   Z,next0   ; 7Fh, DEL: ignored
                              JP   NC,e_hi   ; 80h-FFh: reserved
015A                          ENDIF      
015A   D6 1A                  SUB   1Ah   ; 7Bh-7Eh: -1Eh in all, index 28-31
015C   D6 09        P5B:      SUB   9   ; 5Bh-60h: -4 in all, index 22-27
015E   C6 05        P3A:      ADD   A,5   ; 3Ah-40h: index 15-21
0160                .macro PTABLE,
0160                             ; 
0160                 DB      h_store & 0FFh  ; !
0160                 DB      h_str & 0FFh    ; "
0160                 DB      h_num & 0FFh    ; #
0160                 DB      h_print & 0FFh  ; $
0160                 DB      h_swap & 0FFh   ; %
0160                 DB      h_and & 0FFh    ; &
0160                 DB      h_emit & 0FFh   ; '
0160                 DB      h_open & 0FFh   ; (
0160                 DB      h_close & 0FFh  ; )
0160                 DB      h_mul & 0FFh    ; *
0160                 DB      h_add & 0FFh    ; +
0160                 DB      h_cfetch & 0FFh ; ,
0160                 DB      h_sub & 0FFh    ; -
0160                 DB      h_cstore & 0FFh ; .
0160                 DB      h_div & 0FFh    ; /
0160                 DB      h_dup & 0FFh    ; :
0160                 DB      h_drop & 0FFh   ; ;
0160                 DB      h_lt & 0FFh     ; <
0160                 DB      h_eq & 0FFh     ; =
0160                 DB      h_gt & 0FFh     ; >
0160                 DB      h_key & 0FFh    ; ?
0160                 DB      h_fetch & 0FFh  ; @
0160                 DB      h_def & 0FFh    ; [
0160                 DB      h_break & 0FFh  ; \
0160                 DB      h_ret & 0FFh    ; ]
0160                 DB      h_xor & 0FFh    ; ^
0160                 DB      h_alloc & 0FFh  ; _
0160                 DB      h_grave & 0FFh  ; `
0160                 DB      h_tor & 0FFh    ; {
0160                 DB      h_or & 0FFh     ; |
0160                 DB      h_fromr & 0FFh  ; }
0160                 DB      h_not & 0FFh    ; ~
0160                .endm
0160                 
0160                             ; Punctuation: A = the PTAB index. The handler starts with HL = TOS,
0160                             ; untouched, and A, DE free.
0160   C6 7C        PUNCT:    ADD   A,PTAB & 0FFh   ; PTAB never crosses a page
0162   5F                     LD   E,A   
0163   16 03                  LD   D,PTAB / 256   ; (0 if the table is in page zero)
0165   FE 92                  CP   (PTAB & 0FFh) + NPG1   ; carry: one of the first NPG1
0167   1A                     LD   A,(DE)   
0168   5F                     LD   E,A   ; the handler's low byte
0169                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-TABP0)   
                              LD   D,0   
0169                          ENDIF      
0169                          IFN   CPM   
                              RL   D   ; its page: 0 + carry
0169                          ENDIF      
0169                          IF   CPM   
0169   16 01                  LD   D,1   
016B   30 01                  JR   NC,pu1   
016D   14                     INC   D   ; its page: 1 + carry
016E                PU1:         
016E                          ENDIF      
016E   D5                     PUSH   DE   ; jump to it; the stack is balanced again
016F   C9                     RET      ;   when the handler starts
0170                             ; The rest of the startup: here so that the generic reset code can reach it
0170                             ; with JR. st0: find the program's NUL; the heap starts after it.
0170                             ; (The editor build has its own copy of this, next to the editor.)
0170                             ; A checked build first clears the lower half of the letter page (A = 0):
0170                             ; every variable starts at 0, every word cell holds 0000h, the address an
0170                             ; undefined word is caught at (see e_hi), and no key is held back.
0170                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)*CHECKED   
                    INIT:     LD   HL,LET   
                    INI1:     LD   (HL),A   
                              INC   L   
                              JP   P,ini1   ; +00h to +7Fh
                              LD   BC,PROG   ; the IP
0170                          ENDIF      
0170                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)   
                    ST0:      LD   H,B   
                              LD   L,C   
                              XOR   A   
                    ST1:      CP   (HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              JR   NZ,st1   
0170                          ENDIF      
0170                          IF   1-EDITOR   
0170   22 7C 07     ST2:      LD   (HEAP),HL   
0173                          ENDIF      
0173                          IF   CHECKED*(1-EDITOR)   
                              RST   20h   ; minus the heap"s first address: "_' may not
                              LD   (NPEND),HL   ;   release below it
0173                          ENDIF      
0173                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*(1-EDITOR)*(1-CPM)   
                              LD   H,A   ; (A = 0) no key is held, and the break key
                              LD   L,A   ;   is on (the checked build has cleared
0173                          ENDIF      ;   these)
0173                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*(1-EDITOR)*CPM   
0173   21 00 00               LD   HL,0   
0176                          ENDIF      
0176                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*(1-EDITOR)   
0176   22 7A 07               LD   (KEYBUF),HL   
0179                          ENDIF      
0179                          IF   1-EDITOR   
0179   D9                     EXX      
017A   21 E0 05               LD   HL,RSTOP   ; the return stack is empty
017D   D9                     EXX      
017E   F7                     RST   30h   ; (its return address is thrown away)
017F                          ENDIF      
017F                             ; In the unchecked generic editor build the table is here, in the first
017F                             ; page, which saves loading D twice. (The other builds have no room for it
017F                             ; here: theirs is further down.)
017F                          IF   TABP0   
                    PTAB:        
                              ;*Macro unroll:  PTABLE
                              DB   h_store & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_str & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_num & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_print & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_swap & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_and & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_emit & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_open & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_close & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_mul & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_add & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_cfetch & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_sub & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_cstore & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_div & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_dup & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_drop & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_lt & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_eq & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_gt & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_key & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_fetch & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_def & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_break & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_ret & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_xor & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_alloc & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_grave & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_tor & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_or & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_fromr & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_not & 0FFh   
                    PTABEND:      
017F                          ENDIF      
017F                             ; =============================================================================
017F                             ;  Handlers that must start in the image's first page: ^ _ ` | ~
017F                             ;  (00bbIGFuZCA= are up among the RST routines.) The machine-code call, exec,
017F                             ;  is here too: it belongs to "`" and makes the page come out right.
017F                             ; =============================================================================
017F   D1           H_XOR:    POP   DE   
0180   7C                     LD   A,H   
0181   AA                     XOR   D   
0182   67                     LD   H,A   
0183   7D                     LD   A,L   
0184   AB                     XOR   E   
0185   6F                     LD   L,A   
0186   F7                     RST   30h   
0187   D1           H_OR:     POP   DE   
0188   7C                     LD   A,H   
0189   B2                     OR   D   
018A   67                     LD   H,A   
018B   7D                     LD   A,L   
018C   B3                     OR   E   
018D   6F                     LD   L,A   
018E   F7                     RST   30h   
018F   E7           H_NOT:    RST   20h   ; ~x = -x - 1
0190   2B                     DEC   HL   
0191   F7                     RST   30h   
0192                             ; "_" ( n -- addr ): the heap pointer moves by n, a signed count (the add is
0192                             ; the same either way); TOS is the old pointer.
0192   ED 5B 7C 07  H_ALLOC:   LD   DE,(HEAP)   
0196                          IF   CHECKED*CPM   
                              LD   A,H   ; the count's sign, for chkhp
0196                          ENDIF      
0196   19                     ADD   HL,DE   ; the new top
0197                          IF   CHECKED   
                              CALL   chkhp   
0197                          ENDIF      
0197   22 7C 07               LD   (HEAP),HL   
019A   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
019B   F7                     RST   30h   
019C   D9           EXEC:     EXX      
019D   22 34 07               LD   (RSAVE),HL   ; machine code may change the alternates
01A0   D9                     EXX      
01A1   CD 2B 01               CALL   jphl   
01A4   D9                     EXX      
01A5   2A 34 07               LD   HL,(RSAVE)   
01A8   D9                     EXX      
01A9   E1                     POP   HL   
01AA   F7                     RST   30h   
01AB                             ; ---- the letters and digits (here, in the middle, so that the inner loop's
01AB                             ; ---- short jumps reach them, and the handlers after them reach rpushn) ------
01AB                             ; Digits: step back onto the first digit and read the whole number.
01AB   E5           DIGIT:    PUSH   HL   
01AC   0B                     DEC   BC   
01AD   CD 1F 03               CALL   rdnum   
01B0   F7                     RST   30h   
01B1                             ; a-z: push the cell's address (the cell is the variable)
01B1   E5           LOWER:    PUSH   HL   
01B2   87                     ADD   A,A   
01B3   6F                     LD   L,A   
01B4   26 07                  LD   H,LETPAGE   
01B6   F7                     RST   30h   
01B7                             ; A-Z: call the word. The return address (the IP after the letter) goes on
01B7                             ; the return stack, and the IP becomes the address in the letter's cell.
01B7   C5           UPPER:    PUSH   BC   ; the return address, for rpushn
01B8   EB                     EX   DE,HL   ; park TOS
01B9   87                     ADD   A,A   
01BA   6F                     LD   L,A   
01BB   26 07                  LD   H,LETPAGE   ; HL -> cell
01BD   4E                     LD   C,(HL)   
01BE   2C                     INC   L   
01BF   46                     LD   B,(HL)   ; IP = the word's body
01C0   EB                     EX   DE,HL   ; TOS back, and fall into rpushn
01C1                             ; rpushn: move the top cell of the data stack (in memory) to the return
01C1                             ; stack, then next. Everything that pushes the return stack ends here.
01C1                             ; 
01C1                             ; The break key is looked at here, so at every word call and loop-back (and
01C1                             ; block entry and "{"), but only one time in 256: B', which nothing else
01C1                             ; uses, counts them. Reading the keyboard can be slow (it is a BDOS call
01C1                             ; under CP/M), and this way it costs a loop four bytes and 14 T-states.
01C1                             ; (DEC B, not DJNZ: its zero flag lasts through the EXX, so one EXX serves
01C1                             ; both ways out.)
01C1   D9           RPUSHN:   EXX      
01C2   D1                     POP   DE   
01C3   2B                     DEC   HL   
01C4   72                     LD   (HL),D   
01C5   2B                     DEC   HL   
01C6   73                     LD   (HL),E   
01C7   05                     DEC   B   
01C8   D9                     EXX      
01C9   CC AE 03               CALL   Z,pollk   
01CC   F7                     RST   30h   
01CD                             ; ---- machine code: the grave -----------------------------------------------
01CD                             ; "`" plus a hex digit loads bytes: ( addr -- addr' ). Pairs of hex digits
01CD                             ; are stored from addr until a non-hex character; then a RET (C9h) is
01CD                             ; written and its address is left. An odd last digit is consumed and dropped.
01CD                             ; "`" plus anything else calls the machine code at TOS: ( addr -- ). The
01CD                             ; code is entered by CALL with the data stack above the return address; it
01CD                             ; must keep BC, and on return the top cell becomes the new TOS.
01CD   CD 9C 03     H_GRAVE:   CALL   hexc   
01D0   30 CA                  JR   NC,exec   
01D2   77           HX1:      LD   (HL),A   ; the high digit goes in first ...
01D3   CD 9C 03               CALL   hexc   
01D6   30 08                  JR   NC,hx2   ; odd digit: consumed, and the RET below
01D8   ED 6F                  RLD      ;   overwrites it
01DA   23                     INC   HL   ; ... and RLD shifts it up under the low one
01DB   CD 9C 03               CALL   hexc   
01DE   38 F2                  JR   C,hx1   
01E0   36 C9        HX2:      LD   (HL),0C9h   ; (never range-checked: the spec says so)
01E2   F7                     RST   30h   
01E3                             ; ---- where the two pages meet ----------------------------------------------
01E3                             ; The first page ends somewhere among the next four handlers, ] \ [ @ (they
01E3                             ; are in falling code order for this), and where exactly differs between the
01E3                             ; builds: NPG1 follows. Every handler below these four must start in the
01E3                             ; second page, and every one above in the first; chktab.py checks both.
01E3                             ; "]" returns: pop an address and jump to it.
01E3   CF           H_RET:    RST   08h   
01E4   42                     LD   B,D   
01E5   4B                     LD   C,E   
01E6   F7           BRK1:     RST   30h   
01E7                             ; "\" ( flag -- ): true skips to the next ")" or "]" at this level; ")"
01E7                             ; drops the block start, "]" returns. No closer at all ends the program.
01E7   7C           H_BREAK:   LD   A,H   
01E8   B5                     OR   L   
01E9   E1                     POP   HL   
01EA   28 FA                  JR   Z,brk1   
01EC   CD 41 03               CALL   skip   
01EF   B7                     OR   A   ; skip returns 0 for ")"
01F0   20 F1                  JR   NZ,h_ret   
01F2   CF           RDROP:    RST   08h   
01F3   F7                     RST   30h   
01F4                             ; "[" followed by a letter stores the body"s address in that letter"s cell:
01F4                             ; uppercase is a word, lowercase a variable. Followed by a space it pushes
01F4                             ; the body"s address instead. Either way it then skips to the matching "]'.
01F4                             ; (The unchecked build takes anything that is not a letter as the space; the
01F4                             ; checked build stops on it.)
01F4   0A           H_DEF:    LD   A,(BC)   
01F5   03                     INC   BC   
01F6   D6 41                  SUB   "A"   ; a letter gives 0-25 or 32-57: lowercase
01F8   5F                     LD   E,A   ;   lands 64 bytes up
01F9   E6 DF                  AND   0DFh   ; fold case
01FB   FE 1A                  CP   26   
01FD   30 0B                  JR   NC,def2   ; not a letter
01FF   CB 23                  SLA   E   
0201   16 07                  LD   D,LETPAGE   ; DE -> cell
0203   79                     LD   A,C   
0204   12                     LD   (DE),A   
0205   1C                     INC   E   
0206   78                     LD   A,B   
0207   12                     LD   (DE),A   
0208   18 03                  JR   skipnx   
020A                DEF2:        
020A                          IF   CHECKED   
                              LD   A,E   
                              CP   " "-"A"+256   
                              JP   NZ,e_brack   ; anything but a letter or a space
020A                          ENDIF      
020A   E5                     PUSH   HL   ; an anonymous block: push its address
020B   60                     LD   H,B   
020C   69                     LD   L,C   
020D                SKIPNX:      
020D                          IF   CHECKED   
                              DEC   BC   ; back onto the letter, so that skip finds its
020D                          ENDIF      ;   opener, the "[", just before where it starts
020D   CD 41 03     SKIPO:    CALL   skip   
0210   F7                     RST   30h   
0211   5E           H_FETCH:   LD   E,(HL)   ; "@"
0212   23                     INC   HL   
0213   56                     LD   D,(HL)   
0214   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
0215   F7                     RST   30h   
0216                             ; =============================================================================
0216                             ;  Handlers that must start in the image's second page.
0216                             ;  "?" is the last (with "," inside it), so its long tail may run past that
0216                             ;  page.
0216                             ; =============================================================================
0216                             ; "(" ( flag -- ): true pushes the block start and enters; false skips to
0216                             ; the matching ")".
0216   7C           H_OPEN:   LD   A,H   
0217   B5                     OR   L   
0218   E1                     POP   HL   
0219   28 F2                  JR   Z,skipo   
021B   C5                     PUSH   BC   ; the block starts at the IP
021C   18 A3                  JR   rpushn   
021E                             ; ")" ( flag -- ): true jumps back to the block start (and keeps it); false
021E                             ; drops it and carries on.
021E   7C           H_CLOSE:   LD   A,H   
021F   B5                     OR   L   
0220   E1                     POP   HL   
0221   28 CF                  JR   Z,rdrop   
0223   CF                     RST   08h   ; pop the block start ...
0224   42                     LD   B,D   
0225   4B                     LD   C,E   
0226   C5                     PUSH   BC   
0227   18 98                  JR   rpushn   ; ... and push it back
0229                             ; ---- arithmetic and logic: ( NOS TOS -- result ) ---------------------------
0229                             ; "-" has two jobs: directly before a digit it starts a negative number.
0229   0A           H_SUB:    LD   A,(BC)   
022A   D6 30                  SUB   "0"   
022C   FE 0A                  CP   10   
022E   38 04                  JR   C,negnum   
0230   E7                     RST   20h   ; a - b = a + (-b): fall into "+"
0231   D1           H_ADD:    POP   DE   
0232   19                     ADD   HL,DE   
0233   F7                     RST   30h   
0234   E5           NEGNUM:   PUSH   HL   ; a negative number: read it, negate it
0235   CD 1F 03               CALL   rdnum   
0238   E7                     RST   20h   
0239   F7                     RST   30h   
023A   D1           H_AND:    POP   DE   
023B   7C                     LD   A,H   
023C   A2                     AND   D   
023D   67                     LD   H,A   
023E   7D                     LD   A,L   
023F   A3                     AND   E   
0240   6F                     LD   L,A   
0241   F7                     RST   30h   
0242                             ; Signed compares. Both are "HL < DE" for the right pair: "<" swaps the two
0242                             ; cells first. Flipping both sign bits turns a signed compare into an
0242                             ; unsigned one (and XOR clears the carry for SBC); SBC HL,HL then turns the
0242                             ; carry into -1 or 0 with no branch.
0242   E3           H_LT:     EX   (SP),HL   ; a < b: HL = a, and b is popped next
0243   D1           H_GT:     POP   DE   ; a > b  is  b < a: HL = b, DE = a
0244   7C                     LD   A,H   
0245   EE 80                  XOR   80h   
0247   67                     LD   H,A   
0248   7A                     LD   A,D   
0249   EE 80                  XOR   80h   
024B   57                     LD   D,A   
024C   ED 52                  SBC   HL,DE   ; carry if HL < DE
024E   ED 62        TF:       SBC   HL,HL   ; carry -> -1 or 0
0250   F7                     RST   30h   
0251   D1           H_EQ:     POP   DE   
0252   B7                     OR   A   
0253   ED 52                  SBC   HL,DE   
0255   7C                     LD   A,H   
0256   B5                     OR   L   
0257   FE 01                  CP   1   ; carry only if a - b = 0
0259   18 F3                  JR   tf   
025B                             ; "*": shift-and-add, 16 rounds; only the low 16 bits are kept. The
025B                             ; multiplier shifts up through A:C.
025B   D1           H_MUL:    POP   DE   ; DE = multiplicand
025C   C5                     PUSH   BC   
025D   7C                     LD   A,H   
025E   4D                     LD   C,L   ; A:C = multiplier
025F   21 00 00               LD   HL,0   
0262   06 10                  LD   B,16   
0264   29           MUL1:     ADD   HL,HL   
0265   CB 21                  SLA   C   
0267   17                     RLA      
0268   30 01                  JR   NC,mul2   
026A   19                     ADD   HL,DE   
026B   10 F7        MUL2:     DJNZ   mul1   
026D   C1                     POP   BC   
026E   F7                     RST   30h   
026F                             ; "/" ( a b -- q r ): the remainder is on top. Truncates toward zero; r takes
026F                             ; a's sign. Divide |a| by |b|, then q gets the sign of a XOR b and r the sign
026F                             ; of a. Dividing by zero returns two cells of no meaning; the checked build
026F                             ; stops on it.
026F                H_DIV:       
026F                          IF   CHECKED   
                              LD   A,H   
                              OR   L   
                              JP   Z,e_zero   
026F                          ENDIF      
026F   D1                     POP   DE   ; DE = a, HL = b
0270   C5                     PUSH   BC   ; free BC for udiv
0271   D5                     PUSH   DE   ; a, for r's sign
0272   7A                     LD   A,D   
0273   AC                     XOR   H   
0274   F5                     PUSH   AF   ; S flag = sign of q
0275   CB 7C                  BIT   7,H   
0277   C4 20 01               CALL   NZ,neg16   ; HL = |b|
027A   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
027B   CB 7C                  BIT   7,H   
027D   C4 20 01               CALL   NZ,neg16   ; HL = |a|, DE = |b|
0280   CD F9 02               CALL   udiv   ; HL = q, DE = r
0283   F1                     POP   AF   
0284   FC 20 01               CALL   M,neg16   ; q's sign
0287   EB                     EX   DE,HL   ; HL = r, DE = q
0288   F1                     POP   AF   ; A = a's high byte
0289   B7                     OR   A   
028A   FC 20 01               CALL   M,neg16   ; r's sign
028D   C1                     POP   BC   
028E   D5                     PUSH   DE   ; q under r
028F   F7                     RST   30h   
0290                             ; ---- stack and storage -----------------------------------------------------
0290   E5           H_DUP:    PUSH   HL   ; ":"
0291   F7                     RST   30h   
0292   E3           H_SWAP:   EX   (SP),HL   ; "%"
0293   F7                     RST   30h   
0294                             ; (The checked build tests the address before it takes the value off the
0294                             ; stack, so that an error report shows both.)
0294                H_CSTORE:      ; "." ( c addr -- )
0294                          IF   CHECKED   
                              CALL   chkst   
0294                          ENDIF      
0294   D1                     POP   DE   
0295   73                     LD   (HL),E   
0296   DF           H_DROP:   RST   18h   ; ";" is this one byte
0297                H_STORE:      ; "!" ( n addr -- )
0297                          IF   CHECKED   
                              CALL   chkst   
0297                          ENDIF      
0297   D1                     POP   DE   
0298   73                     LD   (HL),E   
0299   23                     INC   HL   
029A   72                     LD   (HL),D   
029B   DF                     RST   18h   
029C                             ; ---- console ---------------------------------------------------------------
029C                             ; 22h pushes the address of the text after it and skips the string.
029C   E5           H_STR:    PUSH   HL   
029D   60                     LD   H,B   
029E   69                     LD   L,C   
029F   CD 36 03               CALL   skipstr   
02A2                          IF   CHECKED   
                              OR   A   ; 0: the text ran out before the closing quote
                              JP   Z,e_quote   
02A2                          ENDIF      
02A2   F7                     RST   30h   
02A3                             ; "$" prints the string at TOS, decoding escapes: "/" plus a character
02A3                             ; clears that character"s bit 6 (/M is CR, /` is space; "/" and ""' have no
02A3                             ; bit 6, so // and /" give themselves).
02A3                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*(1-EDITOR)   
02A3   7E           H_PRINT:   LD   A,(HL)   
02A4   23                     INC   HL   
02A5   FE 22                  CP   22h   
02A7   28 0D                  JR   Z,pr9   
02A9   FE 2F                  CP   "/"   
02AB   20 04                  JR   NZ,pr1   
02AD   7E                     LD   A,(HL)   
02AE   23                     INC   HL   
02AF   E6 BF                  AND   0BFh   
02B1   EF           PR1:      RST   28h   
02B2   18 EF                  JR   h_print   
02B4                          ENDIF      
02B4                          IF   CHECKED   
                                 ; (The checked build has the loop as a routine, prstr, which the error
                                 ; report uses too. The address is kept on the stack meanwhile: a report
                                 ; shows the stack as it was before the "$".)
                    H_PRINT:   PUSH   HL   
                              CALL   prstr   
                              POP   DE   
                              RST   18h   
02B4                          ENDIF      
02B4                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*EDITOR   
                                 ; (With the editor the loop is a routine, prstr, which ^V uses too.)
                    H_PRINT:   CALL   prstr   
                              RST   18h   
02B4                          ENDIF      
02B4   7D           H_EMIT:   LD   A,L   ; "'"
02B5   EF                     RST   28h   
02B6   DF           PR9:      RST   18h   
02B7                             ; "#" prints TOS as a signed decimal number, with no space after it.
02B7   C5           H_NUM:    PUSH   BC   
02B8   CD 62 03               CALL   psgn   
02BB   C1                     POP   BC   
02BC   DF                     RST   18h   
02BD                             ; "?" ( n -- c ) or ( -n -- addr )
02BD                             ;   n > 0: wait about n ms for a key; 0 if none came
02BD                             ;   n = 0: wait for a key
02BD                             ;   n < 0: read a line of at most -n characters, with echo. The buffer
02BD                             ;          holds 127 characters and the CR: a bigger count is taken as 127.
02BD   CB 7C        H_KEY:    BIT   7,H   
02BF   20 19                  JR   NZ,line   
02C1   1E 28        KT1:      LD   E,MSLOOP   ; one millisecond, roughly
02C3   CD DC 03     KT2:      CALL   getk   
02C6   20 0E                  JR   NZ,kt3   
02C8   1D                     DEC   E   
02C9   20 F8                  JR   NZ,kt2   
02CB   7C                     LD   A,H   ; 0? never counts down: it waits
02CC   B5                     OR   L   
02CD   28 F2                  JR   Z,kt1   
02CF   2B                     DEC   HL   
02D0   7C                     LD   A,H   
02D1   B5                     OR   L   
02D2   20 ED                  JR   NZ,kt1   ; A = 0 if the time ran out
02D4   FE                     DB   0FEh   ; (CP n: steps over the one byte of ",")
02D5   7E           H_CFETCH:   LD   A,(HL)   ; "," shares "?"s ending: A becomes TOS
02D6   6F           KT3:      LD   L,A   
02D7   26 00                  LD   H,0   
02D9   F7                     RST   30h   
02DA                          IF   CPM   
02DA                             ; CP/M: BDOS 10 does the editing (the spec allows the platform's
02DA                             ; own line editor). It doesn't store the CR, so it is added here.
02DA   11 7F 00     LINE:     LD   DE,127   ; TOS is minus the count: adding 127 carries
02DD   19                     ADD   HL,DE   ;   only for 1 to 127, and leaves 127 - count
02DE   9F                     SBC   A,A   
02DF   A5                     AND   L   ; (0 for a count that is too big)
02E0   EE 7F                  XOR   127   ; A = the count, 127 at most
02E2   32 7E 07               LD   (LBHDR),A   
02E5   11 7E 07               LD   DE,LBHDR   
02E8   3E 0A                  LD   A,10   
02EA   CD FA 03               CALL   bdosx   
02ED   21 7F 07               LD   HL,LBHDR+1   
02F0   7E                     LD   A,(HL)   ; the count typed (0-127)
02F1   2C                     INC   L   ; HL = LINEBUF, whose low byte is 80h:
02F2   85                     ADD   A,L   ;   adding the count to L can't carry
02F3   6F                     LD   L,A   
02F4   36 0D                  LD   (HL),13   
02F6                          ENDIF      
02F6                          IFN   CPM   
                                 ; Generic: Backspace takes the last character back (and is echoed as
                                 ; it is), CR ends (stored, not echoed), every other key is stored and
                                 ; echoed until the line is full. The line buffer starts at offset 80h
                                 ; of its page, so L alone is the place in the line: D holds the L of
                                 ; a full line.
                    LINE:     LD   DE,127   ; TOS is minus the count: adding 127 carries
                              ADD   HL,DE   ;   only for 1 to 127, and leaves 127 - count
                              SBC   A,A   
                              AND   L   ; (0 for a count that is too big)
                              CPL      
                              LD   D,A   ; D = the L of a full line: 80h + count, FFh
                                 ;   at most
                              LD   HL,LINEBUF   
                    LN2:      CALL   getk   
                              JR   Z,ln2   
                              CP   13   
                              JR   Z,ln5   
                              CP   8   
                              JR   Z,ln4   
                              LD   E,A   
                              LD   A,L   
                              CP   D   
                              JR   Z,ln2   ; full
                              LD   (HL),E   
                              INC   L   
                              LD   A,E   
                    LN3:      RST   28h   
                              JR   ln2   
                    LN4:      DEC   L   ; Backspace: one back, and echo it,
                              JP   M,ln3   ;   unless the line was empty (L left the
                              INC   L   ;   upper half of the page)
                              JR   ln2   
                    LN5:      LD   (HL),A   ; the CR
02F6                          ENDIF      
02F6   2E 80                  LD   L,LINEBUF & 0FFh   
02F8   F7                     RST   30h   
02F9                             ; =============================================================================
02F9                             ;  More routines (no handler starts past this point)
02F9                             ; =============================================================================
02F9                             ; udiv: unsigned HL / DE (DE <= 8000h). Returns HL = quotient, DE = remainder.
02F9                             ; Uses A, BC; the caller saves the IP. The dividend shifts up through A:C
02F9                             ; while the quotient bits arrive at the bottom of C.
02F9                             ; Dividing by 2 is one shift (the spec wants that fast).
02F9   7B           UDIV:     LD   A,E   
02FA   EE 02                  XOR   2   
02FC   B2                     OR   D   
02FD   20 07                  JR   NZ,udv0   
02FF   CB 3C                  SRL   H   
0301   CB 1D                  RR   L   ; the quotient
0303   8F                     ADC   A,A   
0304   5F                     LD   E,A   ; the remainder: the bit that fell out (D is 0)
0305   C9                     RET      
0306   7C           UDV0:     LD   A,H   
0307   4D                     LD   C,L   
0308   21 00 00               LD   HL,0   
030B   06 10                  LD   B,16   
030D   CB 21        UDV1:     SLA   C   
030F   17                     RLA      
0310   ED 6A                  ADC   HL,HL   
0312   ED 52                  SBC   HL,DE   ; carry is clear here: the remainder
0314   30 02                  JR   NC,udv2   ;   always fits in 16 bits
0316   19                     ADD   HL,DE   ; too much: put it back, and cancel the
0317   0D                     DEC   C   ;   INC below
0318   0C           UDV2:     INC   C   ; a quotient bit
0319   10 F2                  DJNZ   udv1   
031B   EB                     EX   DE,HL   ; DE = remainder
031C   67                     LD   H,A   
031D   69                     LD   L,C   ; HL = quotient
031E   C9                     RET      
031F                             ; rdnum: read decimal digits at IP into HL; IP is left on the first
031F                             ; non-digit. Values wrap at 16 bits, as the spec says.
031F   21 00 00     RDNUM:    LD   HL,0   
0322   0A           RDN1:     LD   A,(BC)   
0323   D6 30                  SUB   "0"   
0325   FE 0A                  CP   10   
0327   D0                     RET   NC   
0328   03                     INC   BC   
0329   54                     LD   D,H   
032A   5D                     LD   E,L   
032B   29                     ADD   HL,HL   
032C   29                     ADD   HL,HL   
032D   19                     ADD   HL,DE   
032E   29                     ADD   HL,HL   ; HL * 10
032F   5F                     LD   E,A   
0330   16 00                  LD   D,0   
0332   19                     ADD   HL,DE   
0333   18 ED                  JR   rdn1   
0335                             ; skipstr: IP is inside a string; step past its closing quote. "/" escapes
0335                             ; the next character, so "/"" does not end it. Leaves A = 22h.
0335                          IF   1-CHECKED   
0335   03           SS0:      INC   BC   
0336   0A           SKIPSTR:   LD   A,(BC)   
0337   03                     INC   BC   
0338   FE 2F                  CP   "/"   
033A   28 F9                  JR   Z,ss0   
033C   FE 22                  CP   22h   
033E   20 F6                  JR   NZ,skipstr   
0340   C9                     RET      
0341                          ENDIF      
0341                          IF   CHECKED   
                                 ; The checked build never steps over a NUL: if the text runs out first it
                                 ; returns A = 0 with the IP on the NUL.
                    SKIPSTR:   LD   A,(BC)   
                              OR   A   
                              RET   Z   
                              INC   BC   
                              CP   22h   
                              RET   Z   
                              CP   "/"   
                              JR   NZ,skipstr   
                              LD   A,(BC)   ; the escaped character
                              OR   A   
                              RET   Z   
                              INC   BC   
                              JR   skipstr   
0341                          ENDIF      
0341                             ; skip: read past text to the closer at this level, and return A = 0 if it
0341                             ; was ")" and 2 if it was "]". Brackets of both kinds count together;
0341                             ; strings are stepped over whole. A NUL first ends the program (for "\" with
0341                             ; no closer; anything else that runs into the NUL had unbalanced brackets
0341                             ; anyway). D counts the open levels, starting at 1 for the one we are in:
0341                             ; skip sets it to 0 and falls through the INC that an opener comes back to.
0341                             ; 
0341                             ; The checked build also looks at the character the skip was started by,
0341                             ; which is always the one just before where it starts: "(" must end at ")",
0341                             ; "[" at "]", and neither may run into the NUL (N); a string with no closing
0341                             ; quote counts as running into it. "\" takes either closer. IX keeps the
0341                             ; place where the skip started, for the report.
0341                SKIP:        
0341                          IF   CHECKED   
                              PUSH   BC   
                              POP   IX   
                              DEC   BC   
                              LD   A,(BC)   
                              INC   BC   
                              LD   E,A   ; E = the opener: ( [ or \
0341                          ENDIF      
0341   16 00                  LD   D,0   
0343   14           SK3:      INC   D   ; an opener: one deeper
0344   0A           SK1:      LD   A,(BC)   
0345                          IF   1-CHECKED   
0345   03                     INC   BC   
0346   B7                     OR   A   
0347   CA 00 00               JP   Z,SKEND   ; (the end of the program)
034A                          ENDIF      
034A                          IF   CHECKED   
                              OR   A   
                              JR   Z,sk6   ; (the IP stays on the NUL)
                              INC   BC   
034A                          ENDIF      
034A   FE 22                  CP   22h   
034C   CC 36 03               CALL   Z,skipstr   ; leaves A = 22h, which matches nothing below
034F   D6 28                  SUB   "("   ;   (or 0, and then the NUL is read next)
0351   28 F0                  JR   Z,sk3   
0353   3D                     DEC   A   ; ")"
0354   28 08                  JR   Z,sk4   
0356   D6 32                  SUB   "["-")"   
0358   28 E9                  JR   Z,sk3   
035A   FE 02                  CP   "]"-"["   
035C   20 E6                  JR   NZ,sk1   
035E   15           SK4:      DEC   D   
035F                          IF   1-CHECKED   
035F   C8                     RET   Z   ; the closer at this level
0360   18 E2                  JR   sk1   
0362                          ENDIF      
0362                          IF   CHECKED   
                              JR   NZ,sk1   
                              LD   D,A   ; the closer at this level: 0 or 2. Bit 1 of the
                              XOR   E   ;   opener is 0 for "(" and 1 for "[", and only
                              AND   6   ;   "\" has bit 2: so this is 2 for the wrong
                              CP   2   ;   closer, and only then
                              LD   A,D   
                              RET   NZ   
                              JR   sk7   
                    SK6:      BIT   2,E   ; the text ran out:
                              JP   NZ,SKEND   ;   "\" with no closer ends the program
                    SK7:      PUSH   IX   ; N. The place is the opener
                              POP   BC   
                              LD   A,"N"   
                              JP   errp   ; (errp drops skip's return address)
0362                          ENDIF      
0362                             ; psgn: print HL as a signed number. Uses BC.
0362   CB 7C        PSGN:     BIT   7,H   
0364   28 04                  JR   Z,pdec   
0366   3E 2D                  LD   A,"-"   
0368   EF                     RST   28h   
0369   E7                     RST   20h   
036A                             ; pdec: print HL unsigned, by recursion on HL / 10 (the stack holds digits).
036A                             ; Uses BC.
036A   11 0A 00     PDEC:     LD   DE,10   
036D   CD F9 02               CALL   udiv   ; HL = HL / 10, E = the last digit
0370   7B                     LD   A,E   
0371   F5                     PUSH   AF   
0372   7C                     LD   A,H   
0373   B5                     OR   L   
0374   C4 6A 03               CALL   NZ,pdec   
0377   F1                     POP   AF   
0378   C6 30                  ADD   A,"0"   
037A   EF                     RST   28h   
037B   C9                     RET      
037C                             ; =============================================================================
037C                             ;  Dispatch table: the low byte of each handler's address, in code order
037C                             ;  (the table itself is the macro PTABLE, defined above the dispatcher).
037C                             ;  It must not cross a page (the dispatcher only adds to its low byte).
037C                             ; =============================================================================
037C                             ; The handlers of the first NPG1 characters start in the image's second page.
037C                             ; ] \ [ @ sit where the two pages meet, and which side each lands on
037C                             ; differs between the builds, so the count is worked out here.
037C                             ; (One division to a line: asm80 only rounds down when it stores a value.)
037C                PGRET:    EQU   (h_ret-BASE)/256   ; 0 = first page, 1 = second
037C                PGBRK:    EQU   (h_break-BASE)/256   
037C                PGDEF:    EQU   (h_def-BASE)/256   
037C                PGFET:    EQU   (h_fetch-BASE)/256   
037C                NPG1:     EQU   21 + PGFET + PGDEF + PGBRK + PGRET   
037C                          IF   1-TABP0   
037C                PTAB:        
037C                          ;*Macro unroll:  PTABLE
037C   97                     DB   h_store & 0FFh   
037D   9C                     DB   h_str & 0FFh   
037E   B7                     DB   h_num & 0FFh   
037F   A3                     DB   h_print & 0FFh   
0380   92                     DB   h_swap & 0FFh   
0381   3A                     DB   h_and & 0FFh   
0382   B4                     DB   h_emit & 0FFh   
0383   16                     DB   h_open & 0FFh   
0384   1E                     DB   h_close & 0FFh   
0385   5B                     DB   h_mul & 0FFh   
0386   31                     DB   h_add & 0FFh   
0387   D5                     DB   h_cfetch & 0FFh   
0388   29                     DB   h_sub & 0FFh   
0389   94                     DB   h_cstore & 0FFh   
038A   6F                     DB   h_div & 0FFh   
038B   90                     DB   h_dup & 0FFh   
038C   96                     DB   h_drop & 0FFh   
038D   42                     DB   h_lt & 0FFh   
038E   51                     DB   h_eq & 0FFh   
038F   43                     DB   h_gt & 0FFh   
0390   BD                     DB   h_key & 0FFh   
0391   11                     DB   h_fetch & 0FFh   
0392   F4                     DB   h_def & 0FFh   
0393   E7                     DB   h_break & 0FFh   
0394   E3                     DB   h_ret & 0FFh   
0395   7F                     DB   h_xor & 0FFh   
0396   92                     DB   h_alloc & 0FFh   
0397   CD                     DB   h_grave & 0FFh   
0398   2C                     DB   h_tor & 0FFh   
0399   87                     DB   h_or & 0FFh   
039A   1C                     DB   h_fromr & 0FFh   
039B   8F                     DB   h_not & 0FFh   
039C                PTABEND:      
039C                          ENDIF      
039C                             ; hexc: if the character at IP is a hex digit (0-9, A-F, a-f), step over it
039C                             ; and return its value in A with the carry set; otherwise leave the IP and
039C                             ; return with the carry clear.
039C   0A           HEXC:     LD   A,(BC)   
039D   D6 30                  SUB   "0"   
039F   FE 0A                  CP   10   
03A1   38 09                  JR   C,hc1   
03A3   E6 DF                  AND   0DFh   
03A5   D6 11                  SUB   11h   
03A7   FE 06                  CP   6   
03A9   D0                     RET   NC   
03AA   D6 F6                  SUB   0F6h   ; + 10, and sets the carry
03AC   03           HC1:      INC   BC   
03AD   C9                     RET      
03AE                             ; =============================================================================
03AE                             ;  Console layer. rawk is the host's key routine: a waiting key in A (zero
03AE                             ;  flag clear), or A = 0 with the zero flag set when none is waiting. putc
03AE                             ;  (RST 28h) prints A. Both keep BC, DE, HL and HL'. In the generic build
03AE                             ;  they are the host's KEY and CONOUT routines themselves.
03AE                             ; 
03AE                             ;  A running program reads the keyboard only through getk and pollk, which
03AE                             ;  between them give the break key its rules:
03AE                             ;    - Ctrl-C stops the program;
03AE                             ;    - any other key that the break check reads is held in KEYBUF for the
03AE                             ;      next "?", and a newer one takes its place;
03AE                             ;    - "?" (getk) takes the held key first;
03AE                             ;    - a program that has stored a non-zero byte at BRKOFF gets Ctrl-C as a
03AE                             ;      key like any other, but two of them within about 250 ms still stop it.
03AE                             ;  Both are called straight from a handler, never from a routine under one:
03AE                             ;  the checked build's report counts on finding one return address above the
03AE                             ;  data stack.
03AE                             ; =============================================================================
03AE                          IFN   CPM   
                    RAWK:     EQU   KEY   
03AE                          ENDIF      
03AE                             ; pollk: the break check (see rpushn).
03AE   CD EC 03     POLLK:    CALL   rawk   
03B1   C8                     RET   Z   ; no key
03B2   32 7A 07               LD   (KEYBUF),A   ; held for the next "?"
03B5   FE 03        PK1:      CP   3   ; (getk joins here)
03B7   C0                     RET   NZ   
03B8                             ; ctlc: Ctrl-C has been read. If the break key is on, that is the end. If
03B8                             ; the program has turned it off, wait about 250 ms for one more key: a
03B8                             ; second Ctrl-C is the end too; any other key is held (the newest wins),
03B8                             ; and the Ctrl-C goes to the program: returns A = 3, zero flag clear.
03B8   3A 7B 07     CTLC:     LD   A,(BRKOFF)   
03BB   B7                     OR   A   
03BC   CA 15 01     CT0:      JP   Z,brk   
03BF   D5                     PUSH   DE   
03C0   11 10 27               LD   DE,250*MSLOOP   
03C3   CD EC 03     CT1:      CALL   rawk   
03C6   20 05                  JR   NZ,ct2   
03C8   1B                     DEC   DE   
03C9   7A                     LD   A,D   
03CA   B3                     OR   E   
03CB   20 F6                  JR   NZ,ct1   
03CD   D1           CT2:      POP   DE   ; A = the second key, or 0 if none came
03CE   FE 03                  CP   3   
03D0   28 EA                  JR   Z,ct0   ; (the zero flag takes the JP there)
03D2   B7                     OR   A   
03D3   28 03                  JR   Z,ct3   
03D5   32 7A 07               LD   (KEYBUF),A   
03D8   3E 03        CT3:      LD   A,3   
03DA   B7                     OR   A   
03DB   C9                     RET      
03DC                             ; getk: a key for "?", or A = 0 and the zero flag if there is none.
03DC   E5           GETK:     PUSH   HL   ; a held key goes first, and is taken out of
03DD   21 7A 07               LD   HL,KEYBUF   ;   the buffer
03E0   7E                     LD   A,(HL)   
03E1   36 00                  LD   (HL),0   
03E3   E1                     POP   HL   
03E4   B7                     OR   A   
03E5   C0                     RET   NZ   
03E6   CD EC 03               CALL   rawk   
03E9   C8                     RET   Z   
03EA   18 C9                  JR   pk1   ; Ctrl-C? If not, that is the key
03EC                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*(1-EDITOR)   
03EC                BRK:      EQU   endprog   ; the unchecked build stops without a word
03EC                          ENDIF      ;   (with the editor, both stacks are cleared);
03EC                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*EDITOR   
                    BRK:      EQU   edit0   
03EC                          ENDIF      
03EC                          IF   CHECKED   
                    BRK:      EQU   e_break   ;   the checked build reports B
03EC                          ENDIF      
03EC                          IF   CPM   
03EC   3E FF        RAWK:     LD   A,0FFh   ; BDOS 6 with E = FFh: a key, or 0
03EE                             ; putc: BDOS 6 for every character. BDOS 2 would check for ^S while
03EE                             ; printing and could swallow a key that BDOS 6 then never sees.
03EE   D5           PUTC:     PUSH   DE   
03EF   E5                     PUSH   HL   
03F0   5F                     LD   E,A   
03F1   3E 06                  LD   A,6   
03F3   CD FA 03               CALL   bdosx   
03F6   E1                     POP   HL   
03F7   D1                     POP   DE   
03F8   B7                     OR   A   ; (for getk)
03F9   C9                     RET      
03FA                             ; bdosx: call BDOS function A with DE, keeping BC and HL'
03FA   C5           BDOSX:    PUSH   BC   
03FB   D9                     EXX      
03FC   E5                     PUSH   HL   
03FD   D9                     EXX      
03FE   4F                     LD   C,A   
03FF   CD 05 00               CALL   BDOS   
0402   D9                     EXX      
0403   E1                     POP   HL   
0404   D9                     EXX      
0405   C1                     POP   BC   
0406   C9                     RET      
0407                          ENDIF      
0407                             ; =============================================================================
0407                             ;  Checked build: the checks and the error report
0407                             ; =============================================================================
0407                          IF   CHECKED   
                                 ; chkstk: both stacks are checked once per character, not in every handler.
                                 ; The data stack is right when SP lies in the 256 bytes below DSTOP: adding
                                 ; the constant carries if it is above (cells were popped that were never
                                 ; pushed), and leaves a high byte of FFh if it is in range. Errors are found
                                 ; a character late at most: the bytes above DSTOP and the guard band below
                                 ; the page take what happens meanwhile. DE is free between characters.
                    CHKSTK:   EX   DE,HL   
                              LD   HL,(1-DSTOP)&0FFFFh   ; (SP is 2 lower here: the call)
                              ADD   HL,SP   
                              EX   DE,HL   
                              JR   C,e_under   
                              INC   D   
                              JR   NZ,e_over   
                              EXX      ; the return stack: in its page (or it has
                              LD   A,H   ;   overflowed), and not above its empty
                              CP   RSPAGE   ;   position (an underflow stays inside the
                              LD   A,L   ;   page, in the guard band)
                              EXX      
                              JR   NZ,e_rover   
                              CP   RSTOP&0FFh+1   
                              RET   C   
                              EXX      ; return stack underflow: it counts as empty
                              LD   L,RSTOP&0FFh   ;   (H is right: the pointer is in its page)
                              EXX      
                              LD   A,"r"   
                              JR   errp   
                    E_ROVER:   LD   A,"R"   ; return stack overflow
                              DB   11h   ; (LD DE,nn hides the next entry)
                    E_OVER:   LD   A,"S"   ; data stack overflow
                              JR   errp   
                    E_UNDER:   LD   SP,DSTOP   ; data stack underflow: it counts as empty
                              LD   A,"s"   
                              JR   error   
                                 ; e_hi: the inner loop read a reserved byte, 80h-FFh: X. But a word cell that
                                 ; was never defined still holds 0000h, and the byte there is a reserved one
                                 ; in every build (AFh or C3h): if the IP is in page zero, this was a call of
                                 ; an undefined word. The call is undone, so the place is the call itself.
                    E_HI:     INC   B   
                              DJNZ   e_resv   ; (B is as it was, and is not 0)
                              RST   08h   
                              LD   B,D   
                              LD   C,E   
                              LD   A,"U"   
                              JR   error   
                                 ; chkhp: HL = the new heap top, DE = the old one, the carry is from adding
                                 ; the count. Stop if the top is not below the limit page, or is below the
                                 ; program's end.
                    CHKHP:       
0407                          ENDIF      
0407                          IF   CHECKED*CPM   
                                 ; With this much room a top that wrapped round can land back in
                                 ; range, so the add is tested too: growing (A, the count's high
                                 ; byte, is positive) must not carry, and releasing must.
                              RRA      ; the carry comes in above the sign:
                              ADD   A,40h   ;   bit 7 = carry XOR sign
                              ADD   A,A   
                              JR   C,e_heap   
                              LD   A,(0007h)   
                              DEC   A   
                              CP   H   
                              JR   C,e_heap   
0407                          ENDIF      
0407                          IF   CHECKED*(1-CPM)   
                                 ; (Here the program's space is under 32K, so a top that wrapped
                                 ; round always falls outside it.)
                              LD   A,H   
                              CP   HEAPLIM   
                              JR   NC,e_heap   
0407                          ENDIF      
0407                          IF   CHECKED   
                              PUSH   DE   
                              EX   DE,HL   
                              LD   HL,(NPEND)   
                              ADD   HL,DE   ; carry: at or above the program's end
                              EX   DE,HL   
                              POP   DE   
                              RET   C   
                    E_HEAP:   OR   A   ; put the count back in TOS for the report
                              SBC   HL,DE   
                              LD   A,"H"   
                              JR   errp   
                                 ; chkst: stop unless HL is in the program's own space: from the letter page
                                 ; up to the heap limit (the OS, or HEAPLIM), so the interpreter's stacks and
                                 ; whatever lies above the limit are safe. Memory above the heap top but
                                 ; below the limit is the program's own: Tiny BASIC keeps its lines there.
                                 ; It is the page of HL + 1 that is tested, so that one test serves both
                                 ; bytes of a cell: the last byte below the limit can"t be stored to with ".'.
                                 ; Keeps HL and BC. It runs on into its own error entry.
                    CHKST:    INC   HL   
                              LD   A,H   
                              DEC   HL   
                              CP   LETPAGE   
                              JR   C,e_store   
0407                          ENDIF      
0407                          IF   CHECKED*(1-CPM)   
                              CP   HEAPLIM   
                              RET   C   
0407                          ENDIF      
0407                          IF   CHECKED*CPM   
                              LD   E,A   
                              LD   A,(0007h)   ; the BDOS page is the heap limit
                              DEC   A   
                              CP   E   
                              RET   NC   
0407                          ENDIF      
0407                          IF   CHECKED   
                                 ; Error entries. Each loads its letter and then hides the next entry inside
                                 ; a 3-byte LD DE,nn (the 11h), so they all fall through to `error`.
                    E_STORE:   LD   A,"O"   ; a store outside the program's space
                              DB   11h   
                    E_BREAK:   LD   A,"B"   ; Ctrl-C (found inside pollk or getk)
                                 ; errp: an error found inside a routine: drop its return address first.
                    ERRP:     POP   DE   
                              JR   error   
                    E_QUOTE:   LD   B,H   ; an unclosed string: HL is its address, one
                              LD   C,L   ;   past the opening quote, which is the place
                              LD   A,"Q"   
                              DB   11h   
                    E_RESV:   LD   A,"X"   ; a reserved byte outside a string
                              DB   11h   
                    E_ZERO:   LD   A,"Z"   ; dividing by zero
                              DB   11h   
                    E_BRACK:   LD   A,"W"   ; bad character after [
                                 ; error: the report, then the end. A = the letter, BC = one past the place,
                                 ; HL = TOS, and both stacks as the report is to show them:
                                 ; 
                                 ;   Err X @ line,col
                                 ;   up to 16 characters of the text from the place
                                 ;   Stk n: the top 8 cells at most, bottom to top
                                 ;   Rtn n
                    ERROR:    PUSH   HL   ; now the whole data stack is in memory
                              LD   E,A   
                              CALL   pnl   
                              DB   "Err ",22h   
                              LD   A,E   
                              RST   28h   
                              CALL   pmsg   
                              DB   " @ ",22h   
                              DEC   BC   ; BC = the place
                                 ; The line and column. A place below the program is in the line
                                 ; buffer: line 0. Otherwise count the LFs from the program's start;
                                 ; DE = the line's number, HL = where it starts.
                              LD   HL,LINEBUF   
                              LD   DE,0   
                              LD   A,B   
                              CP   PROG/256   
                              JR   C,er3   
                              INC   H   
                              LD   L,E   ; HL = PROG
                    ER1:      INC   DE   ; a new line starts at HL
                              PUSH   HL   
                    ER2:      LD   A,L   
                              SUB   C   
                              LD   A,H   
                              SBC   A,B   
                              JR   NC,er2x   ; reached the place
                              LD   A,(HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              CP   10   
                              JR   NZ,er2   
                              POP   AF   
                              JR   er1   
                    ER2X:     POP   HL   
                    ER3:      PUSH   BC   
                              PUSH   HL   
                              EX   DE,HL   
                              CALL   pdec   ; the line
                              LD   A,","   
                              RST   28h   
                              POP   DE   
                              POP   HL   
                              PUSH   HL   
                              OR   A   
                              SBC   HL,DE   
                              INC   HL   
                              CALL   pdec   ; the column
                              CALL   pnl   
                              DB   22h   
                              POP   HL   ; the text, as it is: 16 characters, or fewer
                              LD   B,16   ;   if the line or the program ends first
                    ER4:      LD   A,(HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              OR   A   
                              JR   Z,er5   
                              CP   13   
                              JR   Z,er5   
                              CP   10   
                              JR   Z,er5   
0407                          ENDIF      
0407                          IF   CHECKED*CPM   
                              CP   1Ah   ; (the ^Z that pads a file's last record ends
                              JR   Z,er5   ;   the text too: some terminals clear the
0407                          ENDIF      ;   screen on it)
0407                          IF   CHECKED   
                              RST   28h   
                              DJNZ   er4   
                    ER5:         ; (without the editor: on into pstk)
0407                          ENDIF      
0407                          IF   CHECKED*EDITOR   
                              CALL   pstk   
                              CALL   pnl   
                              DB   22h   
                              JP   edit0   ; back to the editor, with both stacks cleared
0407                          ENDIF      
0407                             ; =============================================================================
0407                             ;  Routines that the checked build's report and the editor share
0407                             ; =============================================================================
0407                SPADJ:    EQU   2*EDITOR   ; (with the editor pstk is called, not fallen
0407                             ;   into: the stack is one address deeper)
0407                          IF   CHECKED+EDITOR   
                                 ; pstk: the two stack lines:  Stk n: the top 8 cells at most, bottom to top
                                 ;                             Rtn n
                                 ; TOS must be in memory with the rest (pushed). In a build without the
                                 ; editor this is the end of `error`, which runs on into it.
                    PSTK:     CALL   pnl   
                              DB   "Stk ",22h   
                              LD   HL,(2+SPADJ-DSTOP)&0FFFFh   ; SP - (DSTOP-2) is minus twice the
                              ADD   HL,SP   ;   depth (the cell at DSTOP-2 was pushed
                              RST   20h   ;   with the first value and holds nothing)
                              CALL   phalf   ; the depth
                              LD   A,":"   
                              RST   28h   
                              LD   A,C   
                              CP   9   
                              JR   C,er6   
                              CALL   pmsg   
                              DB   " ...",22h   
                              LD   C,8   
                    ER6:      LD   H,0   ; C = the number of cells to show
                              LD   L,C   
                              ADD   HL,HL   
                              ADD   HL,SP   ; HL -> just above the deepest of them
0407                          ENDIF      
0407                          IF   EDITOR   
                              INC   HL   
                              INC   HL   
0407                          ENDIF      
0407                          IF   CHECKED+EDITOR   
                              INC   C   
                    ER7:      DEC   C   
                              JR   Z,er8   
                              DEC   HL   
                              LD   D,(HL)   
                              DEC   HL   
                              LD   E,(HL)   
                              PUSH   HL   
                              PUSH   BC   
                              LD   A," "   
                              RST   28h   
                              EX   DE,HL   
                              CALL   psgn   
                              POP   BC   
                              POP   HL   
                              JR   er7   
                    ER8:      CALL   pnl   
0407                          ENDIF      
0407                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*EDITOR   
                              DB   "Rtn 0",22h   ; (only ^V comes here, and at the editor the
                              RET      ;   return stack is always empty)
0407                          ENDIF      
0407                          IF   CHECKED   
                              DB   "Rtn ",22h   
                              EXX      
                              PUSH   HL   
                              EXX      
                              POP   DE   
                              LD   HL,RSTOP   
                              OR   A   
                              SBC   HL,DE   
0407                          ENDIF      
0407                          IF   CHECKED*(1-EDITOR)   
                              CALL   phalf   
                              CALL   pnl   
                              DB   22h   
                              JP   endprog   
0407                          ENDIF      
0407                          IF   CHECKED+EDITOR   
                                 ; phalf: print half of HL, and leave it in C. (With the editor, pstk ends by
                                 ; running on into this.)
                    PHALF:    SRL   H   
                              RR   L   
                              PUSH   HL   
                              CALL   pdec   
                              POP   BC   
                              RET      
                                 ; prstr: print the string at HL, to its closing quote, decoding "/" (this is
                                 ; "$", and the texts of the report and the editor). In the checked build a
                                 ; NUL first is an error: Q.
                    PRSTR:    LD   A,(HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              CP   22h   
                              RET   Z   
0407                          ENDIF      
0407                          IF   CHECKED   
                              OR   A   
                              JR   Z,e_dollar   
0407                          ENDIF      
0407                          IF   CHECKED+EDITOR   
                              CP   "/"   
                              JR   NZ,prs1   
                              LD   A,(HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              AND   0BFh   
                    PRS1:     RST   28h   
                              JR   prstr   
                                 ; pmsg: print the text that follows the CALL, to its closing quote. Keeps HL.
                                 ; pnl: the same, on a new line.
                    PNL:      LD   A,13   
                              RST   28h   
                              LD   A,10   
                              RST   28h   
                    PMSG:     EX   (SP),HL   
                              CALL   prstr   
                              EX   (SP),HL   
                              RET      
0407                          ENDIF      
0407                          IF   CHECKED   
                    E_DOLLAR:   POP   DE   ; "$" ran into a NUL: drop the return address,
                              POP   HL   ;   and put the string's address back in TOS
                              LD   A,"Q"   
                              JP   error   
0407                          ENDIF      
0407                             ; =============================================================================
0407                             ;  The line editor (EDITOR = 1)
0407                             ; 
0407                             ;  The interpreter starts here, and a program that ends comes back here.
0407                             ;  There is no prompt. It follows the spec's suggested standard for a line
0407                             ;  editor (docs/b8script.md, Environments). Type a line and press Return:
0407                             ; 
0407                             ;    n text    put the text in as line n; the lines from n on move down. A
0407                             ;              number past the end (or 0) adds the line at the end.
0407                             ;    n         take line n out
0407                             ;    anything else is run at once, as B8Script. (Start such a line with a
0407                             ;    space if it would begin with a digit.)
0407                             ; 
0407                             ;  A command key ends the line too, and takes what was typed as its argument:
0407                             ; 
0407                             ;    ^G        run the program
0407                             ;    n ^L      list from line n (no number: all of it). Any key holds the
0407                             ;              list until another key is pressed; Ctrl-C ends it.
0407                             ;    n ^E      put line n in the input line; Return puts it back, changed
0407                             ;    name ^R   read. CP/M: the file of that name (no name: the same file as
0407                             ;              last time). Generic: what is typed, or pasted, from now until
0407                             ;              ^Z replaces the program; it is not echoed.
0407                             ;    name ^W   write. CP/M: to that file (no name: the same file as last
0407                             ;              time). Generic: the text is printed, as it is.
0407                             ;    ^N ^N     new: no program (the key twice in a row)
0407                             ;    ^V        view: the build, both stacks, and the program's size, lines
0407                             ;              and free memory
0407                             ;    ^X        leave (to LEAVE)
0407                             ; 
0407                             ;  In the line: ^B and ^F, or the left and right arrow keys, move the cursor;
0407                             ;  a character goes in at the cursor; Backspace and DEL take out the one
0407                             ;  before it; Esc drops the line. Only CR, LF, BS and printing characters are
0407                             ;  sent to the terminal, so any terminal will do.
0407                             ; 
0407                             ;  Lines are counted, not numbered: the text holds no line numbers, and the
0407                             ;  list shows each line's place. There can be 65535 lines. A typed line holds
0407                             ;  125 characters; the one character after a line number separates it from
0407                             ;  the text and is not stored. The text is kept as it is typed, each line
0407                             ;  ending in CR LF, at PROG.
0407                             ; 
0407                             ;  What lasts from one line to the next: the program, the words, the
0407                             ;  variables and the data stack. An error or a break clears both stacks. The
0407                             ;  return stack starts empty for every line.
0407                             ; 
0407                             ;  Things to know:
0407                             ;    - Reset empties the program (generic builds).
0407                             ;    - A word's address points into the program, so run the program again
0407                             ;      after editing it.
0407                             ;    - Nothing is printed between a program's output and what is typed next.
0407                             ;    - A line run at once sits in the line buffer, which -n? also reads into:
0407                             ;      a line that calls -n? and carries on afterwards runs what was typed.
0407                             ;      (The stored program never comes back to the line, so it may.)
0407                             ;    - The editor"s own keys are not the program"s: -n? is the plain line
0407                             ;      read of the other builds (BDOS 10 under CP/M).
0407                             ; 
0407                             ;  The data stack is the CPU's stack, so the editor works on top of whatever
0407                             ;  the last line left there, with TOS pushed like the rest.
0407                             ; =============================================================================
0407                          IF   EDGEN   
                    INIT:        ; reset (A = 0)
0407                          ENDIF      
0407                          IF   EDGEN*CHECKED   
                                 ; Clear the lower half of the letter page: every variable starts at 0, and
                                 ; every word cell holds 0000h, the address an undefined word is caught at
                                 ; (see e_hi).
                              LD   HL,LET   
                    INI1:     LD   (HL),A   
                              INC   L   
                              JP   P,ini1   ; +00h to +7Fh
0407                          ENDIF      
0407                          IF   EDGEN   
                              JR   edit0   
0407                          ENDIF      
0407                          IF   EDITOR   
                                 ; ^F, right arrow: one to the right, by printing the character there
                    RIGHT:    LD   A,L   
                              CP   E   
                              JR   Z,ed1   ; at the end
                              LD   A,(HL)   
                              INC   L   
                              JR   lf1   
                                 ; Esc: alone it drops the line. An arrow key sends Esc [ and a letter, so
                                 ; wait about 5 ms for a second key: after a "[" read on to the letter that
                                 ; ends the sequence, and act on C (right) and D (left).
                    ESC:      LD   BC,5*MSLOOP   
                    ES1:      CALL   rawk   
                              JR   NZ,es2   
                              DEC   BC   
                              LD   A,B   
                              OR   C   
                              JR   NZ,es1   
                              CALL   fin   ; no second key: the line is dropped
                              JR   edit   
                    ES2:      CP   "["   
                              JR   NZ,ed1   ; not a sequence known here
                    ES3:      CALL   ekey   
                              CP   40h   
                              JR   C,es3   ; (its parameters)
                              SUB   "C"   
                              JR   Z,right   
                              DEC   A   ; "D"?
                              JR   NZ,ed1   ; no: on into left
                                 ; ^B, left arrow: the cursor goes one to the left
                    LEFT:     LD   A,L   
                              ADD   A,A   
                              JR   Z,ed1   ; (L = 80h: at the start)
                              DEC   L   
                              LD   A,8   
                    LF1:      RST   28h   
                              JR   ed1   
                                 ; edit0: reset, an error or a break: both stacks are cleared.
                                 ; skend: a program that ended inside skip: its return address goes.
                                 ; edend: a program that ended: TOS joins the rest of the data stack.
                    EDIT0:    LD   SP,DSTOP-2   ; empty (the cell that stands for TOS is pushed)
                              DB   21h   ; (LD HL,nn: steps over the next two bytes)
                    SKEND:    POP   DE   
                    EDEND:    PUSH   HL   
                                 ; edit: start a new input line.
                    EDIT:     EXX      
                              LD   HL,RSTOP   ; the return stack is empty
                              EXX      
                              LD   HL,0   
                              LD   (KEYBUF),HL   ; no key is held, and the break key is on
                              LD   (EDLN),HL   ; no line is being edited
                              LD   HL,LINEBUF   ; HL = the cursor,
                              LD   E,L   ;   E = the end of the line (its low byte)
                    ED1:      CALL   ekey   
                              CP   7Fh   
                              JR   Z,bsp   ; DEL
                              CP   " "   
                              JR   NC,insc   
                              CP   9   
                              JR   Z,insc   ; Tab is text
                              CP   8   
                              JR   Z,bsp   
                              CP   2   
                              JR   Z,left   ; ^B
                              CP   6   
                              JR   Z,right   ; ^F
                              CP   1Bh   
                              JR   Z,esc   
                              PUSH   HL   ; a command key? Look it up
                              LD   HL,cmds   
                              LD   B,NCMD   
                    ED2:      CP   (HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              JR   Z,ed3   
                              INC   HL   
                              INC   HL   
                              DJNZ   ed2   
                              POP   HL   
                              JR   ed1   ; no: the key is ignored
                    ED3:      LD   A,(HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              LD   H,(HL)   
                              LD   L,A   
                              EX   (SP),HL   ; the command's address: fin returns to it
                                 ; fin: end the input line: CR LF and a NUL after it, and a new line on the
                                 ; terminal. Leaves BC -> the line and HL -> the NUL.
                    FIN:      LD   H,LETPAGE   
                              LD   L,E   
                              LD   (HL),13   
                              INC   L   
                              LD   (HL),10   
                              DEC   L   
                              CALL   prl   ; (prints the CR LF)
                              LD   (HL),0   
                              LD   BC,LINEBUF   
                              RET      
                                 ; Backspace, DEL: the character before the cursor goes. The cursor moves
                                 ; left, the rest of the line moves down over it, and the last place (now a
                                 ; space) is printed over along with the rest.
                    BSP:      LD   A,L   
                              ADD   A,A   
                              JR   Z,ed1   ; at the start
                              DEC   L   
                              LD   A,8   
                              RST   28h   
                              PUSH   HL   
                    BS1:      INC   L   
                              LD   A,(HL)   
                              DEC   L   
                              LD   (HL),A   
                              INC   L   
                              LD   A,L   
                              CP   E   
                              JR   NZ,bs1   
                              DEC   L   
                              LD   (HL)," "   
                              POP   HL   
                              LD   D,E   
                              DEC   E   
                              JR   ic2   
                                 ; A character goes in at the cursor: it ripples up through the rest of the
                                 ; line, the cursor moves on, and the rest is printed again.
                    INSC:     LD   B,A   
                              LD   A,E   
                              CP   0FDh   
                              JR   Z,ed1   ; the line is full: 125 characters
                              LD   A,B   
                              RST   28h   
                              PUSH   HL   
                    IC1:      LD   A,(HL)   
                              LD   (HL),B   
                              LD   B,A   
                              LD   A,L   
                              INC   L   
                              CP   E   
                              JR   NZ,ic1   
                              POP   HL   
                              INC   L   
                              INC   E   
                              LD   D,E   
                    IC2:      CALL   tail   
                              JR   ed1   
                                 ; tail: print the line from the cursor to D (a low byte), and bring the
                                 ; cursor back with backspaces. Nothing at all if the cursor is at D.
                    TAIL:     LD   C,L   
                    TA1:      LD   A,L   
                              CP   D   
                              JR   Z,ta2   
                              LD   A,(HL)   
                              RST   28h   
                              INC   L   
                              JR   ta1   
                    TA2:      LD   A,L   
                              CP   C   
                              RET   Z   
                              LD   A,8   
                              RST   28h   
                              DEC   L   
                              JR   ta2   
                                 ; ekey: wait for a key
                    EKEY:     CALL   rawk   
                              JR   Z,ekey   
                              RET      
                                 ; The command keys, and where each goes (after fin).
                    CMDS:     DB   13   
                              DW   cret   
                              DB   7   ; ^G
                              DW   crun   
                              DB   12   ; ^L
                              DW   clist   
                              DB   5   ; ^E
                              DW   cedln   
                              DB   18   ; ^R
                              DW   cread   
                              DB   23   ; ^W
                              DW   cwrite   
                              DB   14   ; ^N
                              DW   cnew   
                              DB   22   ; ^V
                              DW   cview   
                              DB   24   ; ^X
                              DW   LEAVE   
                    NCMD:     EQU   9   
                                 ; ^N ^N: no program, if the next key is ^N too
                    CNEW:     CALL   ekey   
                              CP   14   
                              JR   NZ,ged0   
                              XOR   A   
                              LD   (PROG),A   
                    GED0:     JP   edit   
                                 ; ^E: line n goes into the input line, to be changed. EDLN remembers which
                                 ; line it was: Return puts the text back in its place.
                    CEDLN:    CALL   rdnum   
                              PUSH   HL   
                              CALL   find   ; HL -> the line, or the NUL if there is none
                              POP   DE   
                              LD   A,(HL)   
                              OR   A   
                              JR   Z,ged0   
                              LD   (EDLN),DE   
                              LD   DE,LINEBUF   
                    CE1:      LD   A,(HL)   ; copy it, and show it, up to its CR (or LF)
                              CP   13   
                              JR   Z,ce2   
                              CP   10   
                              JR   Z,ce2   
                              LD   (DE),A   
                              RST   28h   
                              INC   HL   
                              INC   E   
                              LD   A,E   
                              CP   0FDh   ; (a longer line is cut at 125 characters)
                              JR   NZ,ce1   
                    CE2:      EX   DE,HL   ; the cursor is at the line's end
                              LD   E,L   
                              JP   ed1   
                                 ; Return. If ^E put a line here, the text goes back in its place. If not:
                                 ; a number and text is a line to put in, a number alone a line to take out,
                                 ; and anything else is run where it is.
                    CRET:     PUSH   HL   ; the end of what was typed
                              LD   HL,(EDLN)   
                              LD   A,H   
                              OR   L   
                              JR   Z,cr1   
                              PUSH   HL   
                              CALL   delln   
                              POP   HL   
                              JR   ins   
                    CR1:      CALL   rdnum   ; HL = the number it starts with, BC -> after
                              LD   A,C   ; C is still 80h if there was no number:
                              ADD   A,A   ;   only then is twice it 0
                              JR   Z,st0p   ; no number: run the line
                              LD   A,(BC)   
                              CP   13   
                              JR   NZ,cr2   
                              POP   DE   ; the number alone: take that line out
                              CALL   delln   
                              JR   gedit   
                    CR2:      INC   BC   ; step over the one character after the number
                                 ; Put the text at BC in as line n (in HL): open a gap of its length there,
                                 ; CR and LF included, and copy it in.
                    INS:      CALL   find   ; HL -> where it goes
                              POP   DE   ; the end of what was typed
                              LD   A,E   
                              SUB   C   ; A = the length of the text, with its CR LF
                              PUSH   BC   ; the text
                              LD   C,A   
                              LD   B,0   
                              PUSH   BC   ; its length
                              LD   D,H   
                              LD   E,L   ; DE = where it goes
                              XOR   A   
                              LD   C,A   ; BC = 0: CPIR looks as far as it needs to
                              CPIR      ; HL -> one past the program's NUL
                              SBC   HL,DE   ; the number of bytes to move up, NUL included
                              LD   B,H   
                              LD   C,L   
                              ADD   HL,DE   
                              DEC   HL   ; HL -> the NUL
                              EX   DE,HL   
                              EX   (SP),HL   ; HL = the length; where it goes is kept
                              PUSH   HL   
                              ADD   HL,DE   ; the NUL's new place
                              EX   DE,HL   
                              LDDR      ; move the rest of the program up
                              POP   BC   ; the length
                              POP   DE   ; where it goes
                              POP   HL   ; the text
                              LDIR      
                    GEDIT:    JP   edit   
                                 ; ^G: run the program. st0p: run the typed line (BC -> it).
                    CRUN:     LD   BC,PROG   
                              DB   3Eh   ; (LD A,n: steps over the POP)
                    ST0P:     POP   HL   ; (the end of what was typed)
                                 ; st0: start running at BC. The heap starts after the stored program's NUL.
                    ST0:      LD   HL,PROG   
                              XOR   A   
                    ST1:      CP   (HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              JR   NZ,st1   
                              LD   (HEAP),HL   
0407                          ENDIF      
0407                          IF   EDITOR*CHECKED   
                              RST   20h   ; minus the heap"s first address: "_' may not
                              LD   (NPEND),HL   ;   release below it
0407                          ENDIF      
0407                          IF   EDITOR   
                              POP   HL   ; TOS: the data stack is as the last line left it
                              RST   30h   ; (its return address is thrown away)
                                 ; ^L: list from line n. DE = the number of the line at HL.
                    CLIST:    CALL   rdnum   ; HL = n, or 0 if there was none:
                              LD   A,H   
                              OR   L   
                              JR   NZ,li0   
                              INC   L   ;   then from line 1
                    LI0:      PUSH   HL   
                              CALL   find   
                              POP   DE   
                    LI1:      LD   A,(HL)   
                              OR   A   
                              JR   Z,gedit   ; the end of the text
                              CALL   rawk   
                              JR   Z,li3   ; no key: carry on
                              CP   3   
                              CALL   NZ,ekey   ; any key but Ctrl-C: wait for one more
                              CP   3   
                              JR   Z,gedit   ; Ctrl-C, first or second, ends the list
                    LI3:      PUSH   HL   
                              PUSH   DE   
                              EX   DE,HL   
                              CALL   pdec   ; the line's number,
                              LD   A," "   
                              RST   28h   ;   a space,
                              POP   DE   
                              POP   HL   
                              INC   DE   
                              CALL   prl   ;   and the line
                              JR   li1   
                                 ; ^V: view.
                    CVIEW:    CALL   pmsg   
                              DB   "B8SZ80E"   
0407                          ENDIF      
0407                          IF   EDITOR*CHECKED   
                              DB   "C"   
0407                          ENDIF      
0407                          IF   EDITOR   
                              DB   " 2026-11-21",22h   
                              CALL   pstk   ; both stacks
                              LD   HL,PROG   
                              LD   DE,0FFFFh   
                    CV1:      INC   DE   ; count the lines, and find the end
                              CALL   nxl   
                              JR   NZ,cv1   
                              PUSH   HL   ; the NUL
                              PUSH   DE   ; the lines
                              LD   DE,(0-PROG)&0FFFFh   
                              ADD   HL,DE   
                              CALL   pnl   
                              DB   "Prog ",22h   
                              CALL   pdec   ; the program's size
                              POP   HL   
                              CALL   pnl   
                              DB   "Lines ",22h   
                              CALL   pdec   
                              POP   DE   
0407                          ENDIF      
0407                          IF   EDGEN   
                              LD   HL,HEAPLIM*256-1   
0407                          ENDIF      
0407                          IF   EDITOR*CPM   
                              LD   A,(0007h)   ; the BDOS page is the limit
                              LD   H,A   
                              LD   L,0   
                              DEC   HL   
0407                          ENDIF      
0407                          IF   EDITOR   
                              OR   A   
                              SBC   HL,DE   
                              CALL   pnl   
                              DB   "Free ",22h   
                              CALL   pdec   ; the room left for text and heap
                              CALL   pnl   
                              DB   22h   
                    GED1:     JP   edit   
                                 ; delln: take line n (in HL) out: copy everything after it down over it.
                    DELLN:    CALL   find   
                              LD   D,H   
                              LD   E,L   
                              CALL   nxl   ; HL -> the next line
                    DE1:      LD   A,(HL)   
                              LD   (DE),A   
                              INC   HL   
                              INC   DE   
                              OR   A   
                              JR   NZ,de1   
                              RET      
                                 ; find: HL = a line number. Returns HL -> that line, or -> the NUL at the end
                                 ; of the text if there are fewer lines (or the number is 0). Keeps BC.
                    FIND:     EX   DE,HL   
                              LD   HL,PROG   
                    FI1:      DEC   DE   
                              LD   A,D   
                              OR   E   
                              RET   Z   
                              CALL   nxl   
                              JR   NZ,fi1   
                              RET      
                                 ; nxl: step HL over one line, to just past its LF (and return not-zero), or
                                 ; stop at the NUL that ends the text (and return zero).
                    NXL:      LD   A,(HL)   
                              OR   A   
                              RET   Z   
                              INC   HL   
                              CP   10   
                              JR   NZ,nxl   
                              OR   A   
                              RET      
                                 ; prl: print the line at HL, to its LF; HL -> just past it.
                    PRL:      LD   A,(HL)   
                              RST   28h   
                              LD   A,(HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              CP   10   
                              JR   NZ,prl   
                              RET      
0407                          ENDIF      
0407                          IF   EDGEN   
                                 ; ^R, generic: what comes in from now until ^Z is the program. A CR is
                                 ; stored as CR LF; a LF right after a line end is dropped (it is the CR's
                                 ; own, or an empty line's), and a LF anywhere else ends a line too. A last
                                 ; line with no end is given one. Nothing is echoed, and there is no check
                                 ; for running out of memory.
                    CREAD:    LD   HL,PROG-1   
                              LD   (HL),10   ; (as if a line had just ended: the byte is
                              INC   HL   ;   the line buffer's last, and spare)
                    RD1:      CALL   ekey   
                              LD   C,A   
                              CP   1Ah   
                              JR   NZ,rd2   
                              LD   A,10   ; ^Z ends the last line, as a LF would
                    RD2:      CP   10   
                              JR   NZ,rd3   
                              DEC   HL   
                              CP   (HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              JR   Z,rd4   ; straight after a line end: dropped
                              LD   A,13   ; anywhere else it ends the line
                    RD3:      LD   (HL),A   
                              INC   HL   
                              CP   13   
                              JR   NZ,rd4   
                              LD   (HL),10   ; after a CR goes a LF
                              INC   HL   
                    RD4:      LD   A,C   
                              CP   1Ah   
                              JR   NZ,rd1   
                              LD   (HL),0   
                              JR   ged1   
                                 ; ^W, generic: the text is printed as it is, for the terminal to capture.
                    CWRITE:   LD   HL,PROG   
                    CW1:      LD   A,(HL)   
                              OR   A   
                              JR   Z,ged1   
                              RST   28h   
                              INC   HL   
                              JR   cw1   
0407                          ENDIF      
0407                          IF   EDITOR*CPM   
                    CFCB:     EQU   005Ch   ; the file's name is kept here, where the CCP
                                 ;   put the one from the command line
                                 ; ^R, CP/M: read the file. A name typed before the key is the file's name
                                 ; from now on.
                    CREAD:    CALL   setname   
                              CALL   load   
                              JP   edit   
                                 ; ^W, CP/M: write the file: delete the old one, make it anew, write the
                                 ; text in records of 128 bytes, and close it. The text's NUL and the 127
                                 ; bytes after it are set to ^Z meanwhile, which pads the last record. (A
                                 ; full disk or directory is not noticed: the calls fail and that is all.)
                    CWRITE:   CALL   setname   
                              LD   C,19   ; delete
                              CALL   fbdos   
                              LD   C,22   ; make
                              CALL   fbdos   
                              LD   HL,PROG   
                              XOR   A   
                    CW1:      CP   (HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              JR   NZ,cw1   
                              DEC   HL   ; HL -> the NUL
                              PUSH   HL   
                              LD   B,128   
                    CW2:      LD   (HL),1Ah   
                              INC   HL   
                              DJNZ   cw2   
                              POP   HL   
                              LD   DE,PROG   
                    CW3:      LD   A,E   ; a record that starts before the end is written
                              SUB   L   
                              LD   A,D   
                              SBC   A,H   
                              JR   NC,cw4   
                              PUSH   HL   
                              LD   C,21   ; write, from where the record lies
                              CALL   frec   
                              POP   HL   
                              JR   cw3   
                    CW4:      LD   (HL),0   ; the NUL again
                              LD   C,16   ; close
                              CALL   fbdos   
                              JP   edit   
                                 ; frec: BDOS function C (read or write a record) with the 128 bytes at DE.
                                 ; Returns A = the BDOS's answer, HL = DE and DE = DE + 128.
                    FREC:     PUSH   DE   
                              PUSH   BC   
                              LD   C,26   ; set the DMA address
                              CALL   BDOS   
                              POP   BC   
                              CALL   fbdos   
                              POP   HL   
                              LD   DE,128   
                              EX   DE,HL   
                              ADD   HL,DE   
                              EX   DE,HL   
                              RET      
                                 ; setname: if a name was typed (the line does not start with its CR), put it
                                 ; in the FCB: up to 8 characters, a dot, up to 3 more, in capitals. The drive
                                 ; is the current one. Then, name or no name, clear the FCB after the name,
                                 ; as it must be before a file is opened or made.
                    SETNAME:   LD   DE,LINEBUF   
                              LD   A,(DE)   
                              CP   13   
                              JR   Z,fcbclr   
                              LD   HL,CFCB   
                              LD   (HL),0   ; the current drive
                              LD   B,11   
                    SN1:      INC   L   
                              LD   (HL)," "   
                              DJNZ   sn1   
                              LD   L,CFCB+1   
                    SN2:      LD   A,(DE)   
                              INC   DE   
                              CP   13   
                              JR   Z,fcbclr   
                              CP   "."   
                              JR   NZ,sn3   
                              LD   L,CFCB+9   ; the type
                              JR   sn2   
                    SN3:      CP   "a"   
                              JR   C,sn4   
                              AND   5Fh   ; a capital
                    SN4:      LD   (HL),A   
                              INC   L   
                              JR   sn2   
                    FCBCLR:   LD   HL,CFCB+12   
                              LD   B,24   
                    FC1:      LD   (HL),0   
                              INC   HL   
                              DJNZ   fc1   
                              RET      
                                 ; fbdos: BDOS function C on the file
                    FBDOS:    LD   DE,CFCB   
                              JP   BDOS   
                                 ; load: read the file into PROG. No such file: no program. The text ends at
                                 ; the file"s first ^Z (1Ah), which pads a text file"s last record; one more
                                 ; goes after the last record, so the search always stops. And every line
                                 ; must end in LF: a last line without one is given a CR LF. (The FCB is
                                 ; clear after its name: the CCP left it so, or setname did.)
                    LOAD:     LD   C,15   ; open (no such file: the first read fails
                              CALL   fbdos   ;   too)
                              LD   DE,PROG   
                    LD1:      LD   C,20   ; read the next 128 bytes
                              CALL   frec   
                              OR   A   
                              JR   Z,ld1   
                              LD   (HL),1Ah   ; (HL = where the record that failed would be)
                              LD   HL,PROG-1   
                              LD   A,10   ; (a file with no text needs nothing added)
                    TR1:      INC   HL   
                              LD   E,A   ; E = the character before this one
                              LD   A,(HL)   
                              CP   1Ah   
                              JR   NZ,tr1   
                              LD   A,E   
                              CP   10   
                              JR   Z,tr2   
                              LD   (HL),13   
                              INC   HL   
                              LD   (HL),10   
                              INC   HL   
                    TR2:      LD   (HL),0   
                              RET      
0407                          ENDIF      
0407                             ; =============================================================================
0407                          IF   CPM   
0407                             ; The RAM pages follow the image; the heap may grow to the BDOS.
0407                START:       
0407                          ENDIF      
0407                          IF   CPM*CHECKED   
                                 ; Clear the lower half of the letter page: every variable starts at
                                 ; 0, every word cell holds 0000h, the address an undefined word is
                                 ; caught at (see e_hi: the byte there is CP/M's JP, C3h), and no key
                                 ; is held back.
                              LD   HL,LET   
                              XOR   A   
                    INI1:     LD   (HL),A   
                              INC   L   
                              JP   P,ini1   ; +00h to +7Fh
0407                          ENDIF      
0407                          IF   CPM   
0407   21 08 01               LD   HL,vecs   ; the RST routines go down into page zero
040A   11 08 00               LD   DE,0008h   
040D   01 2C 00               LD   BC,vecend-vecs   
0410   ED B0                  LDIR      
0412                          ENDIF      
0412                          IF   CPM*EDITOR   
                              CALL   load   ; the file named on the command line
                              JP   edit0   
0412                          ENDIF      
0412                          IF   CPM*(1-EDITOR)   
0412   11 5C 00               LD   DE,005Ch   ; open the file named on the command line
0415   0E 0F                  LD   C,15   ; (no such file: the first read fails too,
0417   CD 05 00               CALL   BDOS   ;   and the program is empty)
041A   11 00 08               LD   DE,PROG   
041D   D5           LD1:      PUSH   DE   
041E   0E 1A                  LD   C,26   ; set the DMA address
0420   CD 05 00               CALL   BDOS   
0423   11 5C 00               LD   DE,005Ch   
0426   0E 14                  LD   C,20   ; read the next 128 bytes
0428   CD 05 00               CALL   BDOS   
042B   E1                     POP   HL   ; HL = the address this record went to
042C   B7                     OR   A   
042D   20 07                  JR   NZ,ld2   
042F   11 80 00               LD   DE,128   
0432   19                     ADD   HL,DE   
0433   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
0434   18 E7                  JR   ld1   
0436   36 00        LD2:      LD   (HL),0   ; the end of the file counts as NUL
0438   23                     INC   HL   ; the heap starts after it
0439   01 00 08               LD   BC,PROG   ; the IP
043C   C3 70 01               JP   st2   
043F                          ENDIF      
043F                          IF   CPM   
043F                             ; RAM pages, after the image
043F                RSPAGE:   EQU   (imgend + 255) / 256   
043F                DSPAGE:   EQU   RSPAGE + 1   
043F                LETPAGE:   EQU   RSPAGE + 2   
043F                PROG:     EQU   LETPAGE*256 + 256   
043F                          ENDIF      
043F                IMGEND:      


